    <item>
      <headword id="idp161827296">monais</headword>
      <description>Notes: ‘coarse woolly twine used for setting up nets to ropes’. SND s.v. monish ‘orig. unascertained’.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161828808">bad</headword>
      <description>Quotation: “We’ll try a bad.” Notes: ‘Shooting overboard 2 or 3 fathoms of net on a breezy night, as a test for presence of herring.’</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161830464">ceannair</headword>
      <description>Notes: the end of the bridle-rope, which is attached to the wing of the net. (Tarbert)</description>
    </item>
  </items>
